  "behaviour": [
    "Selected package skill bodies and context sources identify their retained source path and base directory.",
    "load_skill accepts an optional relative resource for explicitly selected package skills; resolves within the selected package; checks manifest declaration, 64 KiB bound, UTF-8, regular nonsymlink file, size and SHA-256 before returning text.",
    "No unrestricted file-read fallback, source execution or additional network authority. Authored skills retain precedence. Removal preserves selected revision objects; wrong pins and tampering fail without content disclosure.",
    "The wrapper preserves the underlying loader concurrency classification; normal skill loading delegates to that loader."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Dirty Hand uses unreleased Harness via go.work. No final candidate or release qualification.",
    "First built-client journey demonstrates read_file rejecting an external package path; the corrected loader journey reads declared resources without relaxing that boundary. Both are preserved.",
    "An intermediate compile failure from treating tool.Executor as a mutable registry is retained; the implementation now requires the actual registry before replacing its loader.",
    "Broad suite passed before the final concurrency-delegation adjustment; targeted tests and final built-client journey passed afterwards. Seven native/public cases remained skipped in the broad run.",
    "The final journey uses a local deterministic provider and makes three requests with zero paid model calls. It does not prove live-model performance.",
    "Runtime reselection, session persistence and container-specific qualification were not added or established by this change. Numeric coverage, all scenarios and remaining release/live gates stay open."
  ]
}
